{\rtf1\ansi\deff0{\fonttbl{\f0\fswiss Arial;}}\viewkind4\uc1\pard\fs24\b SAP S/4HANA Order-to-Cash (O2C) Functional Design\b0\par\par\pard\fs22\b 1. Document Information\b0\par\pard\fs20 Project Name: SAP S/4HANA Order-to-Cash Transformation\par Document Type: Functional Design Document\par Version: 1.0\par Prepared By: Business and IT Design Team\par Date: 2026-10-08\par Confidentiality: Internal / Client Confidential\par\par\pard\fs22\b 2. Executive Summary\b0\par\pard\fs20 This document defines the functional design for the Order-to-Cash (O2C) process in SAP S/4HANA. The O2C process covers all activities from customer inquiry and sales order creation to delivery, billing, payment, and revenue realization. The objective is to create a streamlined, auditable, and efficient process that improves customer experience, reduces cycle time, supports collection efficiency, and ensures compliance with financial controls.\par\par\pard\fs22\b 3. Business Context\b0\par\pard\fs20 The company sells products and services through direct sales and distribution channels. O2C is critical to revenue generation and cash flow. Current challenges include manual pricing, slow billing, delivery exceptions, weak credit management, and delayed cash application. The target solution in SAP S/4HANA standardizes these functions and improves visibility and process control.\par\par\pard\fs22\b 4. Objectives\b0\par\pard\fs20 - Enable efficient sales order processing from inquiry to cash\par - Ensure correct pricing, taxation, and customer validations\par - Reduce order-to-cash cycle time\par - Improve order, delivery, and invoice visibility\par - Strengthen credit and receivables controls\par - Improve customer satisfaction and collections\par - Support compliance and audit requirements\par\par\pard\fs22\b 5. Scope\b0\par\pard\fs20 In Scope:\par - Customer master and account setup\par - Sales order creation and amendment\par - Pricing and condition records\par - Availability check and order confirmation\par - Delivery processing and goods issue\par - Billing and invoice posting\par - Accounts receivable and payment processing\par - Credit management and dispute handling\par - Returns and credit memos\par - Reporting and transactions monitoring\par\par Out of Scope:\par - Procurement and vendor processes\par - HR or payroll processes\par - Non-O2C functional areas\par\par\pard\fs22\b 6. Functional Process Flow\b0\par\pard\fs20 Customer inquiry or quotation\par -> Customer master validation\par -> Sales order creation\par -> Pricing and tax determination\par -> Availability check and confirmation\par -> Delivery creation and warehouse execution\par -> Goods issue\par -> Billing and invoice posting\par -> Accounts receivable and payment receipt\par -> Credit management and dispute resolution\par -> Returns and credit note management\par\par\pard\fs22\b 7. Business Process Details\b0\par\pard\fs20\b 7.1 Customer Master and Account Setup\b0\par - Maintain customer master data with sales area, company code, and credit control area\par - Maintain billing, shipping, and payment terms\par - Support tax and legal entity data for international customers\par - Use customer hierarchy and partner functions\par\par\b 7.2 Inquiry and Quotation\b0\par - Create inquiry or quotation from customer request\par - Maintain pricing, discounts, freight, and validity dates\par - Route approvals for large discounts or exceptions\par\par\b 7.3 Sales Order Creation\b0\par - Create standard sales orders in SAP S/4HANA\par - Validate customer, material, and pricing data\par - Maintain order changes before delivery\par - Apply item categories and schedule line logic\par\par\b 7.4 Availability Check and Confirmation\b0\par - Perform ATP checks\par - Confirm or partially confirm quantities\par - Identify shortages and backorders\par\par\b 7.5 Delivery Processing\b0\par - Create outbound deliveries from confirmed orders\par - Support partial deliveries and warehouse activities\par - Update shipping and logistics execution status\par\par\b 7.6 Goods Issue and Shipment\b0\par - Post goods issue against delivery\par - Update stock and cost flow\par - Record shipment confirmation and dispatch status\par\par\b 7.7 Billing\b0\par - Generate billing documents from delivery or order\par - Apply tax and pricing logic\par - Manage invoice, credit memo, and debit memo scenarios\par - Publish invoice outputs through print or electronic methods\par\par\b 7.8 Accounts Receivable and Payment\b0\par - Post receivables from billing documents\par - Reconcile incoming customer payments\par - Support partial and residual payments\par - Manage open items and aging\par\par\b 7.9 Credit Management\b0\par - Review customer credit exposure\par - Block orders or deliveries exceeding limits\par - Manage approvals and exception workflows\par\par\b 7.10 Returns and Claims\b0\par - Process return order and delivery\par - Approve refund or credit memo actions\par - Capture return reasons and dispute information\par\par\pard\fs22\b 8. Master Data Requirements\b0\par\pard\fs20 - Customer master\par - Material master\par - Pricing and condition records\par - Tax determination rules\par - Ship-to and bill-to relationships\par - Payment terms\par - Credit control area\par - Sales org, distribution channel, division\par\par\pard\fs22\b 9. Functional Requirements by Role\b0\par\pard\fs20 Sales User\par - Create and update sales orders\par - Validate pricing\par - Monitor order fulfillment\par\par Warehouse / Logistics User\par - Confirm deliveries\par - Post goods issue\par - Resolve shipment exceptions\par\par Billing User\par - Post billing documents\par - Review invoice errors\par - Support invoice output\par\par Finance / AR User\par - Review open items\par - Process incoming payments\par - Handle dispute and cash application exceptions\par\par Credit Manager\par - Manage exposure and credit blocks\par - Approve high-risk exceptions\par\par\pard\fs22\b 10. System and Integration Design\b0\par\pard\fs20 The O2C process in SAP S/4HANA integrates with master data, warehouse, finance, external commerce, payment, and analytics systems. Customer and material master data should be maintained centrally and replicated where required. Invoice and order status updates should be available in real time to downstream systems. Payment and cash application interfaces must be automated where possible.\par\par\pard\fs22\b 11. Business Rules and Controls\b0\par\pard\fs20 - Sales orders cannot be created for blocked customers without credit approval\par - Material master validation before order creation\par - Pricing must follow approved condition tables\par - Billing must be based on valid delivery or service confirmation\par - Tax determination must align with legal and customer location\par - Payment terms must match final commercial agreement\par - Reversals require approval and audit traceability\par - Returns and credits must include reason codes\par - High-value adjustments require formal approval\par\par\pard\fs22\b 12. Exception Handling\b0\par\pard\fs20 Exceptions include blocked orders, stock shortages, billing errors, payment mismatches, claims, and tax disputes. Each exception should have an assigned owner, resolution timeline, and tracking process. Root cause analysis should support continuous process improvement.\par\par\pard\fs22\b 13. Reporting and KPIs\b0\par\pard\fs20 - Open sales orders\par - Order cycle time\par - On-time delivery rate\par - Billing accuracy\par - Invoice aging\par - DSO and collections efficiency\par - Credit exposure\par - Returns and credit memo rate\par - Delivery exception trend\par\par Sample KPI targets:\par - On-time delivery above 95 percent\par - Billing error rate below 1 percent\par - Invoice dispute rate below 2 percent\par - Cash application within agreed SLA\par\par\pard\fs22\b 14. Security and Authorization\b0\par\pard\fs20 Role-based access controls are required. Sales users can create and update orders within assigned areas. AR users can post payments. Credit managers can approve or reject exceptions. Audit logs should capture changes to price, payment, and invoice data.\par\par\pard\fs22\b 15. Non-Functional Requirements\b0\par\pard\fs20 Performance, scalability, reliability, auditability, and compliance are core requirements. The solution must be able to handle transaction growth while maintaining process integrity and financial controls.\par\par\pard\fs22\b 16. SDLC Alignment\b0\par\pard\fs20 Requirements phase: capture process scope and business rules\par Design phase: configure process flow, roles, controls, and integrations\par Build phase: implement SAP configuration and interface logic\par Test phase: validate with unit, integration, and UAT scenarios\par Deployment phase: cutover, hypercare, and training\par Support phase: monitoring, optimization, and enhancements\par\par\pard\fs22\b 17. Risks and Mitigation\b0\par\pard\fs20 Risk: poor master data quality. Mitigation: data cleansing and validation before go-live.\par Risk: delayed collections. Mitigation: clear credit and payment policy.\par Risk: tax or billing errors. Mitigation: automated validation and reconciliation.\par Risk: user adoption issues. Mitigation: role-based training and support.\par\par\pard\fs22\b 18. Acceptance Criteria\b0\par\pard\fs20 - End-to-end O2C process mapped\par - Key master data and controls defined\par - Roles assigned\par - Integration touchpoints documented\par - KPIs approved\par - Test scenarios cover standard and exception flows\par - Stakeholders approve the design\par\par\pard\fs22\b 19. Conclusion\b0\par\pard\fs20 The O2C process in SAP S/4HANA is critical to revenue realization, customer satisfaction, and financial accuracy. This functional design provides a clear framework for implementation, testing, and support in the SAP SDLC lifecycle.\par\par\pard\fs22\b Approval\b0\par\pard\fs20 Business Process Owner\par Finance Lead\par Sales Operations Lead\par IT Solution Architect\par SAP Functional Lead\par Security and Controls Lead\par}\pard\par\par\fs20\b End of Document\b0\par}